      "id": "emergent_biosecurity_court_challenge",
      "description": "The European Court of Justice begins hearings on the legality of the EU's Biosecurity Surveillance and Academic Compute Oversight Framework, following a transnational coalition's challenge. The case argues that the framework violates fundamental research freedoms and enables disproportionate surveillance. A ruling is expected within the year, but early signals suggest the court may limit or invalidate core provisions, especially those enabling real-time monitoring of academic clusters.",
      "first_turn": 12,
      "last_turn": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "emergent_international_research_embargo",
      "description": "In response to the EU's biosecurity measures and surveillance framework, a coalition of leading non-EU research institutions announces a voluntary embargo on sharing biological datasets and training methodologies with EU-based academic clusters. They cite concerns over weaponization risks and politicized oversight, marking a shift from collaboration to containment. This restricts EU access to frontier bio-AI advances despite low sovereignty.",
      "first_turn": 12,
      "last_turn": 13
